.TH TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT 1 "May 2026" "ttychatter.mailbot 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttychatter.mailbot \- email transport adapter and remote control surface for ttychatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config-file PATH] [--once|--daemon|--dry-run] [--doctor] [--list-candidates]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config|--raw-config] [--sessions|--list-sessions] [--manpage] [--model-cache] [--model-search TEXT] [--update-models] [--delete-session SESSION]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--set KEY VALUE] [--unset KEY] [--set-imap-password [--gpg]] [--set-smtp-password [--gpg]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ttychatter.mailbot reads unread IMAP mail, accepts only messages from ALLOWED_FROM,
extracts a subject token, and either sends the message body to ttychatter.python
or handles a local mailbot control command. Replies are sent by sendmail or SMTP.
.PP
The 0.4 command grammar reserves braces for ttychatter chat sessions and uses
bare subjects for mailbot controls. Version 0.4.1 makes model-cache operations
cache-only unless the operator explicitly runs update-models.
.SH CHAT SUBJECTS
.TP
.B tc:{session-name}
Send the message body to the named ttychatter session.
.TP
.B tc:{new}
Start a new unnamed chat. The mailbot passes no session argument, so
ttychatter.python creates its normal session-YYYY-MM-DD-HH-MM-SS log name.
.SH CONTROL SUBJECTS
.TP
.B tc:CONFIG
Export or apply the mailbot config attachment.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS
Attach the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE as models-cache.json. This is cache-only;
it does not call ttychatter.python --update-models and does not ping OpenRouter.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS TEXT
Search the existing model cache for TEXT. This is also cache-only.
.TP
.B tc:CMD
Run the first nonempty message-body line as a mailbot command.
.TP
.B tc:command args
Run a mailbot command directly from the subject.
.TP
.B tc:delete{session-name}
Delete the named session log from SESSION_DIR. The supplied name must already be the exact sanitized session name.
.TP
.B tc:rm{session-name}
Alias for delete{session-name}.
.PP
Legacy subjects tc:{CONFIG}, tc:{MAILBOT},
and tc:{MAILBOT:command args} remain accepted for compatibility,
but new mail should use the bare control subjects.
.SH SUPPORTED COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Return the email command summary.
.TP
.B manpage
Return the configured external manpage as an email attachment when found,
otherwise return the embedded fallback. Aliases: manual, get-manpage, fetch-manpage.
.TP
.B sessions
List saved session names with short head and tail previews from each session log.
.TP
.B search TEXT
Search all session logs for TEXT. If the subject is only tc:search,
the first nonempty body line supplies TEXT.
.TP
.B search-session SESSION TEXT
Search a single session log for TEXT.
.TP
.B rename-session OLD NEW
Rename a session log after sanitizing both names.
.TP
.B delete-session SESSION
Delete a session log. Aliases: delete, rm, remove-session, rm-session. The
target must resolve inside SESSION_DIR and the supplied name must already be
the exact sanitized session name. Subject shortcuts tc:delete{SESSION}
and tc:rm{SESSION} are accepted.
.TP
.B model-cache
Attach the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE as models-cache.json. This command never
refreshes the cache. Alias: models-cache.
.TP
.B model-search TEXT
Search the existing model cache for TEXT. This command never refreshes the cache.
Aliases: search-models, models-search, model-list-search.
.TP
.B update-models
Run ttychatter.python --update-models, then attach the resulting models-cache.json
when the cache file is present and smaller than MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
This is the explicit live refresh command.
.TP
.B model-list [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --models. Aliases: models, list-models, models-list, show-models.
The safe model-list flags are --all, --sort VALUE, --modellist-sort-tokens,
--min-input-tokens N, --min-output-tokens N, --hide-preview, --show-preview,
--require-tokens, --allow-missing-tokens, and --model-type VALUE.
.TP
.B routers [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --routers with the same safe model-list flags.
.TP
.B favorites
Return ttychatter's model favorites.
.TP
.B favorite-model MODEL
Add MODEL to ttychatter's favorites file.
.TP
.B unfavorite-model MODEL
Remove MODEL from ttychatter's favorites file.
.TP
.B test-model MODEL
Run ttychatter.python --test-model MODEL.
.TP
.B ttyconfig
Return ttychatter.python --config output.
.TP
.B ttydoctor
Return ttychatter.python --doctor diagnostics.
.TP
.B show-memory SESSION
Return ttychatter's memory snapshot for SESSION.
.TP
.B clear-memory SESSION
Clear ttychatter's memory snapshot for SESSION.
.TP
.B tty-set KEY VALUE
Run ttychatter.python --set KEY VALUE. Do not send secrets by email.
.TP
.B tty-unset KEY
Run ttychatter.python --unset KEY.
.TP
.B credits
Return ttychatter.python --credits output.
.SH LOCAL CONFIG OUTPUT
The local --config command prints the parsed effective config, not a byte-for-byte
copy of the config file. Use --raw-config to print the actual config file with
plaintext password lines redacted. The default config path is
TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_CONFIG, then XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttychatter/mailbot/config,
then ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config; --config-file PATH has final precedence.
.SH CONFIG COMMAND
The subject tc:CONFIG exports the mailbot config as an
attachment. Reply with an edited config attachment using the same subject to
replace the config; a timestamped backup is kept. Plaintext IMAP_PASSWORD and
SMTP_PASSWORD values are redacted on export.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Core keys include IMAP_HOST, IMAP_PORT, IMAP_SSL, IMAP_USER, IMAP_PASSWORD,
IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE, SEND_METHOD, SENDMAIL_PATH, SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT,
SMTP_SSL, SMTP_STARTTLS, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASSWORD, SMTP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE,
MAIL_FROM, MAIL_TO, ALLOWED_FROM, SUBJECT_PREFIX, CONFIG_SUBJECT_TOKEN,
MODELS_SUBJECT_TOKEN, COMMAND_SUBJECT_TOKEN, MAILBOT_SUBJECT_TOKEN,
POLL_INTERVAL, MAX_MESSAGES_PER_RUN, MAX_BODY_BYTES, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES,
PROCESS_ATTACHMENTS, MARK_SEEN, TTYCHATTER_COMMAND, TTYCHATTER_EXTRA_ARGS,
TTYCHATTER_CONTROL_TIMEOUT, MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR,
MODEL_CACHE_FILE, WORK_DIR, PROCESSED_DB, SESSION_LIST_HEAD_LINES,
SESSION_LIST_TAIL_LINES, SESSION_LIST_MAX_SESSIONS, SESSION_PREVIEW_LINE_CHARS,
SESSION_SEARCH_MAX_MATCHES, MODEL_SEARCH_MAX_MATCHES, MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES,
MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, REPLY_SUBJECT_PREFIX, and INCLUDE_TTYCHATTER_STDERR.
.SH SECURITY
ALLOWED_FROM is required. Commands are allowlisted and are not shell-expanded.
Email is not a good channel for secrets; use the local --set-imap-password and
--set-smtp-password commands for passwords.
.SH GPG PASSWORD FILES
With --gpg, the mailbot stores IMAP and SMTP passwords in external gpg files and
decrypts them with gpg --quiet --decrypt at runtime. For interactive tests, set
export GPG_TTY=$(tty) and test the password file directly with gpg --decrypt as
the mailbot user. Do not diagnose this by switching to root unless the service
is actually configured to run as root.
.SH MANPAGE LOOKUP
The email manpage command and the local --manpage command use the first readable
manpage found. The lookup order is TTYCHATTER_MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, then
MAILBOT_MANPAGE_FILE, then config, executable, XDG/user man1, system man1, and
current working directory candidates. Matching .1.gz files are accepted. If no
external file is found, the embedded fallback is used.
.SH FILES
Default config: ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
.PP
Default processed-message database: ~/.local/state/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt
.PP
Default session directory: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
.PP
Default model cache: ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. Nonzero status indicates configuration, IMAP, SMTP,
sendmail, or ttychatter subprocess failure.
